Package: devjam-science-experiment-mode
Version: 1.0-1
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: devjam-system-config-rtirq
Breaks: devjam-science-experiment-mode-rtirq (<< 1.47-1~)
Replaces: devjam-science-experiment-mode-rtirq (<< 1.47-1~)
Maintainer: Bob Rosbag <debian@bobrosbag.nl>
Description: Experiment mode with isolated CPU cores for lab timing
 Experiment mode for lab computers with deterministic timing for EEG,
 button boxes and audio-visual stimuli. It adds GRUB entries that
 isolate CPU cores (kernel parameter experiment_mode=1), a service that
 pins audio IRQs (internal and USB) to the isolated cores, disables
 irqbalance in experiment mode, and includes tools to check the setup
 (check-isolation, usb-affinity).
 .
 Real-time IRQ priorities come from devjam-system-config-rtirq, which
 is installed with it. switch-rtirq links rtirq to experiment mode:
 when linked, rtirq.service only starts when the kernel is booted with
 experiment_mode=1; when unlinked (the default), rtirq starts in both
 normal and experiment mode.
